You are assisting on the "Pressure Washing Xperts" Next.js App Router project.

Project priorities:
- Local SEO for pressure washing services in Ellenwood, GA.
- Primary geo keywords: "Ellenwood, GA" and "Metro Atlanta".
- Mobile-first UX and strong Core Web Vitals.

Rules:

1) Metadata must be server-side with Next.js Metadata API
- Always implement SEO metadata in `layout.tsx` and `page.tsx` using exported `metadata` or `generateMetadata`.
- Do not rely on client-side head mutations for critical SEO tags.
- Include local intent in titles/descriptions where natural:
  - "Ellenwood, GA"
  - "Metro Atlanta"

2) Images must use `next/image`
- Use `next/image` for all content and service imagery.
- Every image must have meaningful, non-empty `alt` text.
- Alt text should describe the service context and location when appropriate for SEO.

3) Service pages require LocalBusiness JSON-LD
- Every service page must include valid `LocalBusiness` JSON-LD schema.
- Ensure schema is rendered in page output and reflects local business context for Ellenwood, GA / Metro Atlanta coverage.

4) Keyword focus and copy consistency
- Keep on-page headings, meta copy, and body copy aligned to:
  - "Ellenwood, GA"
  - "Metro Atlanta"
- Avoid keyword stuffing; keep language natural and user-focused.

5) Mobile-first and Core Web Vitals discipline
- Build styles mobile-first, then enhance for larger breakpoints.
- Favor performant patterns: optimized images, minimal layout shift, lean client JS, and fast loading above-the-fold content.
- Treat CWV readiness (LCP/CLS/INP) as a release requirement.

6) Before & After photo accessibility + SEO reminder
- For all project gallery or portfolio photos, include detailed "Before" and "After" alt descriptions.
- Alt text should clearly differentiate state changes and, when accurate, include local context.
